21 November 2026 — Reviewed the local 02805 curriculum at the user's request. [Week 7, sentiment measurement and validation](<../../../data/week7/Week 7 · From meaning to measurement · 02805.html#sentiment>) teaches contextual and lexicon sentiment, validation on labelled text and the limits of comparing scores. That directly supports the Guardian measurement and validation. The logistic regression example in Week 7 classifies text. H2b instead uses multiple linear regression to explain a numerical signing-level score. [Week 2, null models](<../../../data/week2/Week 2 · Models & null models — 02805.html#a-null-model-in-action-the-friendship-paradox>) teaches the logic of preserving features while shuffling. H2b applies that logic to age labels within season. The saved curriculum pages reviewed here do not teach H2b's specific covariate-adjusted regression or establish the validity of its shuffle with covariates. The [Week 8 FAQ](<../../../data/week8/Week 8 · Putting it all together · 02805.html#faq>) explicitly permits methods beyond class and asks the paper to centre on the course's network science and NLP. Proposed paper treatment: keep H2b as an optional exploratory extension if its explanation and figure answer a distinct part of the tone question within six pages. Keep the course-taught sentiment validation and before-to-after comparison central. The user has yet to decide whether to retain H2b.

